  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "MediaInfo.Wrapper.Core 26.10.0\n\nMediaInfoLib 26.10, through MediaInfo.Core.Native 26.10.0. Targets netstandard2.1, net8.0, net10.0 (.NET 6 dropped). Previous release: 26.1.0.\n\nADDED\n\n- IMediaInfoAnalyzer: AnalyzeAsync for files, URLs, streams and discs; AnalyzeFolderAsync.\n- DVD and Blu-ray titles and chapters from the navigation tables.\n- MediaInfoAnalyzerBuilder: validation, caching, timeout, retry, concurrency limit, external subtitles.\n- AddMediaInfoAnalyzer for dependency injection.\n- AsLegacy() for code written against MediaInfoWrapper.\n- AudioStream.DynamicObjects, SubtitleStream.MaxCharactersPerLine.\n- VideoStream.Rotation, ScanType, DisplayAspectRatio.\n- More audio, subtitle, video and HDR format identifiers.\n- P/Invoke declarations for the remaining MediaInfoLib exports.\n\nCHANGED\n\n- DTS:X reports 12 channels (7.1.4) instead of 8; its objects are in DynamicObjects.\n- Five-channel Opus is 5.0, not 4.1.\n- MP3 duration and bit rate are more accurate with encoder delay or a Xing header.\n- MediaInfoList.Open honours InfoFileOptions.\n- MediaInfoWrapper is obsolete.\n\nFIXED\n\n- Heap corruption: strings owned by the native library were freed by the runtime.\n- Unicode file names on Linux and macOS.\n- DVD and Blu-ray folder detection on case-sensitive file systems.\n\nLIMITATIONS\n\n- Analyzing a file or a URL cannot be cancelled while the native library opens it.\n\nGuide: https://github.com/yartat/MP-MediaInfo/blob/master/docs/async-api.md\nRelease notes: https://github.com/yartat/MP-MediaInfo/blob/master/docs/release-notes/26.10.0.md",
